] [17592186406922 #edb/ref 1071 "Compute $P(1<X\\le 5)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{18}x,\\, & 0\\le x\\le 6, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406922 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "77d8a3b9-ab3f-5af1-ac16-cd6ceeb35611" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406922 #edb/ref 1074 "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X\\le b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(1<X\\le 5) & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}\\frac{1}{18}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{36}{x}^{2}]}_{1}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406955 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186406970 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406955 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186406971 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406955 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186406972 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406955 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186406973 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406955 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186406974 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406955 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406955 #edb/ref 1045 "The Inverse of an Affine Transformation" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406955 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186406970 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406955 #edb/ref 1048 #edb/ref 17592186046659 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406955 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406955 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "13211b98-9cdf-5456-a254-0f2d03a88cbb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406956 #edb/ref 1080 "A triangle" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406956 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406956 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0fc064fc-557b-51b4-acc4-5e5aac84e9ea" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186406957 #edb/ref 1080 "A l